:"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122870.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #122824\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n```\r\n[gd_scene format=3 uid=\"uid://y30mf816qt5b\"]\r\n\r\n[node name=\"Node\" type=\"Node\" unique_id=70928734]\r\n\r\n[node name=\"Node\" type=\"Node\" parent=\".\" unique_id=709208734]\r\nm\r\n[node name=\"Node1\" type=\"Node\" parent=\".\" unique_id=1613559442]\r\n\r\n[node name=\"Node2\" type=\"Node\" parent=\".\" unique_id=134649808]\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\nOn newline there is no check for `what` not being empty, therefore it builds up to `m[node name` breaking the parser without throwing an error. This leads to the scene partially loading. A simple check fixes the issue.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122870/reactions","total_count":6,"+1":6,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122870/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}